which is $0.7\sigma$ below the steady-cooling value $0.5$. The two routes to $\alpha_{\rm inj}$ — the integrated index with $\Delta=0.5$, and the band-limited index — agree within their uncertainties but do not coincide, and the band-limited route gives the lower Mach number ($M\approx3.3$ rather than $5.9$). This is a second, independent reason why the integrated-index inversion does not robustly determine $M$.

